WEEK 1–2: Python for AI & Automation
Goal: Learn just enough Python to read, clean, and prepare data for AI.
Day 1: Why Python dominates AI — overview of AI landscape + Colab setup
Day 2: Python syntax, loops, and conditional logic — quick coding warm-up
Day 3: Lists, tuples, and dictionaries — how AI stores and manipulates data
Day 4: Functions and lambdas — reusable logic for model steps
Day 5: Classes & OOP basics — modeling “objects” like Data, Model, etc.
Day 6: Reading/writing files (CSV, JSON) — intro to data pipelines
Day 7: Working with APIs using requests — fetching real-world data (e.g., weather or quotes)
Day 8: Virtual environments & dependency control — lightweight project hygiene
Day 9: GitHub essentials — pushing notebooks and collaborating
Day 10: Mini Project: Scrape website data → save as CSV → upload to GitHub
WEEK 3: Data Science & Visualization
Goal: Understand how AI learns from structured data.
Day 11: What is data science and how it fuels AI systems
Day 12: Intro to Numpy — arrays, vectors, and numerical power
Day 13: Pandas basics — loading and exploring CSV data
Day 14: Cleaning data — handle missing values, duplicates, and wrong types
Day 15: Descriptive statistics — spotting trends and correlations
Day 16: Visuals with Matplotlib — plotting patterns AI would “see”
Day 17: Seaborn & Plotly — prettier, interactive charts
Day 18: EDA hands-on: Netflix or IPL dataset exploration
Day 19: Creating an EDA report + basic insights write-up
Day 20: Connecting EDA → ML: how clean data improves predictions
WEEK 4: Machine Learning Foundations
Goal: Learn how machines actually “learn” using scikit-learn.
Day 21: What is Machine Learning — intuition through real examples
Day 22: Supervised learning — regression vs classification explained
Day 23: Data splitting — training, testing, and model validation
Day 24: Preprocessing — scaling, encoding, and cleaning for ML

Day 25: Linear & Logistic Regression — first real models
Day 26: Decision Trees & Random Forest — “how machines make choices”
Day 27: Evaluating models — accuracy, F1, confusion matrix
Day 28: Build & test: predict student marks or housing prices
Day 29: Visualizing feature importance & results
Day 30: Recap + ML in real life (credit scoring, spam filters, etc.)
WEEK 5–6: Deep Learning with TensorFlow or PyTorch
Goal: See how neural networks power modern AI.
Day 31: What is a Neural Network — human brain analogy + visual demo
Day 32: Layers, neurons, activations, and loss — simplified math intuition
Day 33: TensorFlow setup & Sequential API walkthrough
Day 34: Build your first NN: predict handwritten digits
Day 35: CNNs for images — how AI “sees” pictures
Day 36: Cat vs Dog demo — step-by-step training in Colab
Day 37: Overfitting & regularization — why models fail
Day 38: Visualize training with TensorBoard
Day 39: Using GPUs in Colab for faster deep learning
Day 40: Mini Project: Image classifier + accuracy comparison
WEEK 7–8: Transformers, LLMs & Hugging Face
Goal: Explore how ChatGPT-like AI systems work.
Day 41: Evolution from ML → Deep Learning → Transformers
Day 42: How attention & embeddings work (visual demo only)
Day 43: Hugging Face intro — using pre-trained models without coding from scratch
Day 44: Sentiment analysis with DistilBERT — infer emotions from text
Day 45: Fine-tuning demo — customizing BERT on small dataset
Day 46: Hugging Face datasets library — using public data for quick tests
Day 47: Upload your model to Hugging Face Hub
Day 48: Mini Project: Q&A or Sentiment chatbot with HF
Day 49: Real-world LLMs — OpenAI, Anthropic, Perplexity use cases
Day 50: Discussion: model bias, responsible AI, and explainability
WEEK 9: LangChain, Vector DBs & RAG
Goal: Understand how AI retrieves knowledge and builds memory.
Day 51: What is prompt engineering — talking effectively to LLMs
Day 52: LangChain basics — Chains, Tools, and Agents
Day 53: What is RAG — how AI “reads documents” to answer questions
Day 54: Vector databases — how FAISS & Chroma store context
Day 55: Document loaders — PDFs, CSVs, websites
Day 56: Build your own “Chat with PDF” pipeline
Day 57: Connect LLM + FAISS + LangChain for simple chatbot
Day 58: Improve retrieval & responses quality
Day 59: Mini Project: PDF Q&A chatbot
Day 60: Capstone showcase — presentation, reflection, and next steps